HEMSight – Terms of Use (English translation, for information only)

Copyright (c) 2026 Markus Stöhr. All rights reserved.

HEMSight is not open-source software. This repository contains the files needed to
install it – the Compose file, Home Assistant manifests and templates. The program
code itself is distributed solely as a prebuilt container image and is not published
in this repository.

You may:
  - download the published images and run them for your own purposes, private or
    commercial, without a limit on the number of installations;
  - adapt the files in this repository for your own installation.

You may not:
  - redistribute, resell, rent out or offer the images or parts of them as a service;
  - remove or alter copyright or attribution notices;
  - reverse engineer, decompile or disassemble the contained program code, except
    where mandatory law permits – in particular, statutory rights to achieve
    interoperability remain unaffected.

Warranty and liability:
HEMSight is provided without any warranty. It controls devices in your home and is at
an early stage of testing; you run it at your own risk. Liability for damages, lost
profits or data loss is excluded to the extent permitted by law. Liability for intent,
gross negligence and for injury to life, body or health remains unaffected.

The German version prevails. German law applies.
